#: ../../AIDE/Specifications_PF.rst:53
msgid "Specifications for the Prefabricated Series"
msgstr ""

#: ../../AIDE/Specifications_PF.rst:58
msgid "This document describes the standard design, performance, materials, and operating features of AguaClara prefabricated (PF) Series drinking water treatment plants. AguaClara fabricates and supplies PF plants as integrated treatment systems. Unless a feature is identified as optional or project-specific, the features described here are included in the supplied plant. Plant dimensions and certain components are configured for the project design flow, source-water quality, site conditions, and applicable regulatory requirements. The PF plant is designed to produce safe, potable drinking water from source water that may be contaminated with particles, pathogens, and dissolved organics."
msgstr ""

#: ../../AIDE/Specifications_PF.rst:61
msgid "PF Series Application and Design Basis"
msgstr ""

#: ../../AIDE/Specifications_PF.rst:63
msgid "AguaClara drinking water treatment technologies remove turbidity and pathogens from raw water and deactivate remaining pathogens before distribution. AguaClara technologies are best suited for centralized water treatment in communities of at least 200 people. AguaClara technologies are not intended to treat low-turbidity groundwater where the primary contaminants are chemicals such as nitrate, fluoride, or heavy metals. AguaClara technologies are gravity-driven and do not require electricity. When required by the topography, pumps can raise the source water to the elevation necessary for water treatment and water distribution."
msgstr ""

#: ../../AIDE/Specifications_PF.rst:65
msgid "AguaClara treatment technologies include trash and grit removal, flow measurement, chemical dosing, rapid mix, flocculation, floc filter, sedimentation, filtration, and disinfection. The :ref:`floc filter <title_Clarification_Intro>` is a fluidized suspension of flocs located in the bottom of the clarifier. A PF plant can be configured with all of these processes. For source water with turbidity consistently below approximately 2 NTU, a project-specific configuration can omit flocculation, the floc filter, and sedimentation after necessary pilot testing."
msgstr ""

